# Sourced by build-image.sh and start-session.sh.
#
# This is the tracked template. On first run, start-session.sh (and
# build-image.sh, if run standalone) copies this file to project.env and,
# if PROJECT_NAME is left empty, fills it in with the current directory's
# name and writes it back to project.env. That gives each project created
# from this template its own name automatically, with no manual editing.
#
# Set PROJECT_NAME here (or in project.env afterwards) only if you want a
# different image/container name than the directory name.

PROJECT_NAME=""
